<div class="view" id="view-flow">
  <!-- WORK, START TO FINISH (task/3643): ONE page for the backlog and the
       pipeline, which were two pages counting the same work two ways. Every
       piece of work is one card in one of five stages, To do › Building › In
       review › Landing › Landed, read from /api/work alone; the River lens
       draws the stages as columns and the List lens as the backlog's rows.
       Backlog and Pipeline are entries into this page (#work/backlog,
       #work/pipeline), and a project's Work tab is it locked to that
       project. The section is drawn by `wkPaint` (scripts/52-work.js.part)
       and boots saying "not read yet". -->
  <section class="wk" id="wkmain" data-wk="main"><div class="empty">not read yet</div></section>
  <details class="grp" id="wkseams">
    <summary>This week at each seam<span class="gmeta">how work crossed from one stage to the next, forward and back</span></summary>
    <div class="wkfoldbody" id="wkseambody"></div>
  </details>
  <details class="grp" id="wkleft">
    <summary>Leftovers the agents clear<span class="gmeta">records that are not work any more; nothing here waits on you</span></summary>
    <div class="wkfoldbody" id="wkleftbody"></div>
  </details>
  <details class="grp" id="wkelse">
    <summary>The same numbers elsewhere on the console<span class="gmeta">the nav badge, the Home tile and a project’s row read this page’s own count, so they cannot disagree with it</span></summary>
    <div class="wkfoldbody" id="wkelsebody"></div>
  </details>
</div>

